{"success": true, "data": {"stdout": "{"text": "Located along the palm tree-lined Collins Avenue, Ocean Three is a remarkable condominium building nestled on the sandy shores of Sunny Isles Beach.\nSun-drenched open floor plans, stylish interiors, and breathtaking views of the Atlantic Ocean and Intracoastal Waterway are just a few of the many features that await Ocean Three home buyers. Discover the lifestyle of this South Florida residential paradise.\nResidents of Ocean Three are surrounded by the waterfront. Each unit showcases Atlantic Ocean and Intracoastal Waterway views from floor-to-ceiling windows and a spacious balcony, while the building's outdoor amenities \u2014 a sparkling swimming pool, spacious pool deck, tennis court, and courtyard, as well as a rooftop Jacuzzi \u2014 offer a glimpse of the soft sandy beaches and gentle surf.\nJust steps from Ocean Three is the beach itself, a long stretch of sugary white sand with views that rival any tropical destination. Ocean Three offers chairs and towel service for residents, so a day at the beach is as carefree as can be.\nThe resort-style lifestyle is enhanced by Ocean Three's magnificent design. Thanks to architect Sieger Suarez Architectural Partnership, Ocean Three is as glamorous inside as it is outside.\nThough each property may differ in terms of upgrades, a majority of Ocean Three condominiums have sleek marble floors", "doc_id": 0}
{"text": "We are a church community for all ages in Cairns. As part of Churches of Christ in Queensland our desire is to bring the light of Christ to Far North Queensland.\nPraying in tongues is one of the weird things that Christians do. It\u2019s a practice that we find talked about in the New Testament, and it\u2019s a practice that can help you pray. In this message we talk about what praying in tongues is, what to expect, and what we do with tongues as a church. This message is a bonus sixth week as part of the series Five Great Prayers Anyone Can Pray. The post Praying in Tongues appeared first on The Lakes Church Cairns.\n\u201cGod will never give you more than you can handle.\u201d People like to quote this line like it\u2019s in the Bible, but it\u2019s not. And it\u2019s not true. Sometimes the things we have to carry in life are overwhelming and crushing. In those times we can always ask God to help us carry things. This message is part of the series Five Great Prayers Anyone Can Pray. The post Help me carry this appeared first on The Lakes Church Cairns.\nGod offers to give us wisdom if we ask for it. So why don\u2019t we ask for it? And when we finally", "doc_id": 1}
{"text": "Will You Become a Judge for Our Scholarship Programs?\nDeaf and Hard of Hearing Scholarship \u2013 is available to undergraduate college students who are deaf and hard of hearing. This $1,000 scholarship covers books, tuition and supplies.\nCommunicative Disorders Scholarship \u2013 is available to graduate level students studying to become audiologists or speech-language pathologists. This $1,000 scholarship also covers books, tuition and supplies.\nDo you want to learn more about our scholarships and recipients? Click here to visit our website.\nIf you have questions or would like to become a judge, please contact Sertoma Inc. at aellington@sertomahq.org. We\u2019d like to have our judges solidified by March 31, 2018!\nI am a member of the Capitol Area Sertoma Club in PA and am a licensed Audiologist. I would be glad to be a judge for the scholarships.\nThat\u2019s wonderful news! Your support is genuinely appreciated. You will be contacted shortly by Sertoma staff with more information.", "doc_id": 2}
